    "StalkB": { "from": "StalkA", "up": 0.16, "fwd": 0.07 },
    "StalkTip": { "from": "StalkB", "up": 0.05, "fwd": 0.06 },

    "_note_tripod": "Terminals are named *Paw* on purpose: detectMorphology needs exact Pelvis + Chest PLUS a *Tail*/*Paw* bone, and an otyugh has no tail. One foreleg on the centreline, two rear legs mirrored. The centroid has to sit inside THAT triangle, which is why the sac's mass is carried behind the shoulders rather than out over the maw.",
